{start_of_chorus}
[G]Bile them cabbage [C]down, boys,
[G]Bake them hoecakes [D]brown,
The [G]only song that [C]I can sing
Is [G]bile them [D]cabbage [G]down.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[G]Went up on the [C]mountain
[G]To give my horn a [D]blow,
I [G]thought I heard my [C]sweetheart say,
"Yonder [G]comes my [D]beau."[G]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[G]Possum in a [C]'simmon tree,
[G]Raccoon on the [D]ground,
Rac[G]coon says, "You [C]son of a gun,
Shake [G]some of them [D]'simmons [G]down!"
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
